## Objective
Deliver a fully navigable, UI-only Shipments History experience with search, filtering, bulk operations, row actions (including re-ship), and detailed shipment management views. No backend or API calls; use mock data.

## Tech & Standards
- Framework: Next.js 14+ (App Router), TypeScript
- UI: Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- State: Client-only (local state/Zustand if needed)
- Accessibility: ARIA, keyboard support, color contrast
- Transitions: Follow Premium Transitions rule; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Naming: IDs prefixed with `parcego-...`; classes follow BEM-like `parcego-...`
- Data: Mocked; deterministic generators for repeatable demos
- Out of scope: Any Shopify integrations; real API/auth

## Routes & Files
- `app/shipments/page.tsx`: Main listing with search, filters, table, bulk actions
- `app/shipments/[id]/page.tsx`: Detailed shipment page (tabbed)
- `components/shipments/ShipmentsTable.tsx`: Table with selection, sorting, pagination
- `components/shipments/FiltersBar.tsx`: Search input, filters, badges, reset
- `components/shipments/BulkActions.tsx`: Export, Print, Archive, Delete (confirm)
- `components/shipments/QuickViewDrawer.tsx`: Row quick-view (drawer)
- `components/shipments/RowActions.tsx`: View, Re-ship, Print, Download
- `lib/mock/shipments.ts`: Types + mock data generator + helpers

Note: If shadcn components are missing, add: `checkbox`, `table`, `dropdown-menu`, `dialog`, `drawer`, `popover`, `calendar`, `select`, `badge`, `toast`, `tabs`, `separator`.

## Data Model (UI-only)
Use these types for consistency:

```ts
export type ShipmentStatus =
  | "LABEL_CREATED"
  | "SCANNED"
  | "IN_TRANSIT"
  | "OUT_FOR_DELIVERY"
  | "DELIVERED"
  | "FAILED";

export type Shipment = {
  id: string;              // e.g., "ASH-2025-000123"
  trackingNumber: string;  // e.g., "ASH-TRK-ABC12345"
  orderNumber?: string;
  createdAt: string;       // ISO
  updatedAt: string;       // ISO
  service: "Standard" | "Express" | "Same Day";
  courier: "Ashraf" | "DHL" | "FedEx" | "UPS";
  weightKg: number;
  cost: number;
  recipient: {
    name: string;
    email?: string;
    phone?: string;
    address1: string;
    address2?: string;
    city: string;
    state?: string;
    postalCode: string;
    country: string;
  };
  originCountry: string;
  destinationRegion?: "Domestic" | "International";
  status: ShipmentStatus;
  tags?: string[];
  notes?: string;
  labelUrl?: string;
  invoiceUrl?: string;
};
```

Mock generator:
- Generate 120 items across past 90 days
- Distribute statuses realistically (Delivered most frequent)
- Ensure mixed services/couriers/regions
- Provide stable seed for deterministic output

## Listing Page – Layout & Behavior
- Header:
  - Title: “Shipments”
  - Quick metrics (mock): Total, Delivered, In Transit, Failed
- Controls Bar:
  - Search input (placeholder: “Search by ID, tracking, recipient, address…”)
  - Filters:
    - Status (multi-select)
    - Date range (calendar popover)
    - Service (multi-select)
    - Courier (multi-select)
    - Destination Region
    - Price range (min/max)
    - Tags (token input or multi-select)
  - Reset filters
  - Bulk actions button (visible only when rows selected)
  - Export CSV button
- Table:
  - Columns: Select, Shipment ID, Date, Recipient, Service, Courier, Weight, Status (badge), Cost, Actions
  - Sorting: Date, Cost, Status, Service (client-side)
  - Pagination: 10/25/50 per page; next/prev + page numbers
  - Row selection: Checkbox (with shift-click range if feasible)
  - Row actions: View, Quick View, Re-ship, Print Label, Download Docs
- Empty States:
  - No results: Offer to clear filters
  - No shipments (initial): CTA to “Create New Shipment”
- Keyboard & A11y:
  - Search focuses with `/`
  - Table rows focusable; actions reachable via keyboard
  - Bulk actions announce selected count via `aria-live="polite"`

IDs:
- Page root: `parcego-shipments-page`
- Search input: `parcego-shipments-search`
- Filters bar: `parcego-shipments-filters`
- Bulk actions bar: `parcego-shipments-bulk`
- Table root: `parcego-shipments-table`
- Row checkbox: `parcego-shipments-rowchk-{id}`
- Row actions menu: `parcego-shipments-rowactions-{id}`

## Filters – Details
- Status: Badges to toggle + dropdown multi-select; reflect active count
- Date range: From/To with calendar popover and presets (7d, 30d, 90d)
- Service & Courier: Multi-select list with checkmarks
- Destination Region: Segmented control (All/Domestic/International)
- Price range: Two inputs; validate min <= max
- Tags: Multi-select with removable chips

All filters update client-side; URL query sync optional but not required in this phase.

## Bulk Operations
- Available when 1+ rows selected:
  - Export CSV (selected or all on page)
  - Print Labels (selected) – mock action/toast
  - Archive (selected) – mock; visually mark archived if needed
  - Delete (selected) – confirm dialog; non-destructive mock (toast)
- Confirmation dialogs must include counts and sample IDs.

## Row Actions
- View Details: Navigate to `/shipments/[id]`
- Quick View: Open drawer with key details (recipient, address, status, docs)
- Re-ship: Opens confirm dialog then routes to `/create-shipment?from={id}` with mocked prefill
- Print Label: Mock toast; optional open label preview if `labelUrl`
- Download Docs: Mock dropdown (Label, Invoice) with fake links

## Detailed Shipment Page `/shipments/[id]`
- Header: ID, tracking, status badge, quick actions (Re-ship, Print, Download)
- Tabs:
  - Overview: recipient, service, courier, weight, cost, notes
  - Timeline: status milestones (align with tracking timeline alignment rule)
  - Label & Docs: mock links, preview card
  - Activity: mock events list (created, status changes)
  - Payments: mock cost breakdown
- Back button to `/shipments` with ID `parcego-shipments-back-btn`

## Quick View Drawer
- Opens from right; contains:
  - Top: ID, status, updatedAt
  - Sections: Recipient, Service/Courier, Docs, Actions
- Close via Esc, overlay click, or close button

## Transitions & Motion
- Hover states for row and actions (soft shadow/color)
- Drawer/Dialog: fade + slide; use GPU-accelerated transforms
- Staggered list on initial load (subtle)
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`: reduce or disable animations

## Accessibility
- All interactive elements keyboard focusable with visible outlines
- ARIA labels for buttons and menus
- Live regions for selection counts and toasts
- Color contrast minimum AA

## Testing & QA (UI)
- Search narrows results by ID, tracking, recipient, and address fields
- Each filter updates the list; reset clears all
- Sorting toggles asc/desc where applicable
- Pagination changes page size and preserves selection per page
- Bulk select (header checkbox) selects only visible rows
- Bulk actions show accurate counts and confirmations
- Row actions work for multiple sample rows
- Detailed page renders for multiple IDs
- Quick view opens/closes and is keyboard-accessible
- Re-ship routes with the correct `from` query
- Reduced-motion mode disables complex transitions

## Implementation Notes
- Prefer composition: small client components for filters/table/actions
- Keep logic client-side; avoid server components for stateful elements
- Mock data loaded once; memoize derived lists where helpful
- Do not add TODOs; keep code clean and commented only where necessary
- Follow project-wide rules for UI (shadcn), Tailwind, and naming

